      "footnotes": [
        "Notes:—(1) Originally, the interest was to be at 5% and the commission 1/800th. The item in the Belgian list was compiled accordingly. In 1927 the Ministry of Finance decided that beginning from January 1923 the rate of interest was to be 8% instead but that the item for commission was to be cancelled. The figure of the Commission for the Readjustment of Finance is made according to this new understanding and therefore higher.",
        "(2) Compound interest in the Belgian list is computed quarterly, whereas in that of the Commission for the Readjustment of Finance it is semi-annually.",
        "(3) Same explanation as above."
      ],
      "context": "Three Banque Belge pour l'Etranger items are listed with original and outstanding amounts and contraction dates, and are excluded from the inadequately secured category because they are being paid from the salt surplus.",
